ONE-LINE SUMMARY STATEMENTS
-----------------------------------------------------------------

CLAIM UNDER AUDIT: The quantified MBH98 body claim that NH annual temperatures of 1990, 1995 and 1997 each exceed every reconstructed year back to AD 1400 at three standard errors (~99.7 % certainty).

FAILURE LOCATION (provisional): MIXED — minor within-paper (abstract omits explicit 3σ quantifier); primary downstream (citation/PR/assessment conflation with millennial claims and loss of caveats).

GAP TYPE: both (mild source prominence asymmetry + clear downstream inflation/conflation with the 1999 extension and popular restatements).

MAP CONFIDENCE: moderate-to-high for the source itself (direct access to paper text and methods); moderate for the full downstream network (exact citing sentences for the most inflated millennial restatements not exhaustively retrieved). Confidence would be raised by systematic quotation of IPCC TAR chapter text, contemporaneous press releases, and a sample of highly-cited secondary papers that attribute millennial uniqueness specifically to the 1998 paper.

