NOTES FOR PROSECUTORS
-----------------------------------------------------------------

- This map deliberately targets the source’s own quantified claim (Field 6) so that construct-validity and internal-validity audits examine whether the multiproxy CFA method and network actually support the stated 3σ exceedances, rather than auditing a later millennial restatement.
- If a prosecutor wishes to audit the downstream millennial claim instead, that is a separate run; findings about it would not be findings about MBH98 itself.
- The paper is careful about its temporal terminus (AD 1400) and declining skill; the most consequential inflation occurs after the paper leaves the authors’ hands.
- Same-author successor (MBH99) is a different source; treating its millennial claim as inflation of MBH98 is a category error unless a downstream text explicitly cites the 1998 paper for the longer claim (in which case the item is MISATTRIBUTED).

